# Cargo.lock is TRACKED (x1, 2026-09-30). It was inherited from the darktable
# fork, where the C build made a Rust lockfile meaningless, and it was never
# revisited once the Rust workspace became the only shipped product. A
# gitignored lockfile means every build silently re-resolves against crates.io
# and the "same commit" can produce different binaries; `--locked` is now passed
# by CI, the container images and scripts/ci-local.sh. Dependency bumps are
# explicit `cargo update` commits, reviewed like any other change.
*~
